  "intro": {
    "en": "Today we go to the coast. At high tide on an estuary, thousands of waders gather on the last bits of dry land, and there's nothing quite like it. Waders are birds with long legs and bills, which feed in the mud and the shallows.\n\nThey are among the hardest birds for beginners: lots of brown, grey and white, and a lot of birds that look alike. To keep it simple we look at five, each with an obvious feature: the huge curved bill, the red legs, the black belly, the white sprinter, the orange legs.\n\nAt the end there's a quiz of ten questions, with birds from the last two lessons mixed in."
  },
