    "title": {
      "en": "Dunlin or Sanderling?"
    },
    "text": {
      "en": "Look at the colour and where they are. A Sanderling in winter is very pale: silver-grey above and snow-white below, and it runs along the waves on a sandy beach. A Dunlin is browner and greyer, with a drooping bill, and feeds in the mud of an estuary."
    }
